> I'd say no.  However, they use different words for counting different
> things (IIRC, at least in Japan, you use different words for "three"...

No cases, but Mandarin uses a kind of counting words, like japanese. In
English you have "two pieces of paper" or "ten loaves of bread", but
*every* noun in Chinese has a measuring/counting word like "pieces" or
"loaves" -- you can't simply say "five apples" or "one dragon".



